Library Structure and Integration Workflow
The library consists of seven headers. TemporalTypes.mqh and TemporalConfig.mqh hold the shared enumerations, the result structure, and the policy. CTemporalDependency.mqh and CDependencyTracker.mqh record the declared inputs, and CTemporalValidator.mqh applies the rules. CTemporalAudit.mqh orchestrates the audit, while CCausalityReport.mqh prints the results.
Figure 3. Flow of recorded dependencies through the audit pipeline
The trading code works with CTemporalAudit through four methods: BeginDecision(), AddDependency(), Audit(), and GetResult(). The orchestrator owns a dependency tracker, a validator, and the result array. Its BeginDecision() resets the tracker and also clears earlier results.
