Scenarios 1 and 5 pass because every input comes from a bar that closed before the decision. Scenario 2 references a bar opening at 12:40, so Rule 1 fires before Rule 2 sees the negative shift. Scenario 3 is the H1 case from Figure 1, rejected by Rule 4. In scenario 4, the decision is at 10:00, and the value is declared as available at 10:05 for a bar that ended at 10:00. A value from that bar is available at 10:00, so Rule 5 rejects the declaration before Rule 7 is reached.
